PRETABLE 16 -- #529 crimewidthkill, REPAIR 16.  Written 2026-09-26 BEFORE any build or probe run of this table (a first
draft of this file, for a 222-row probe, was replaced in place before anything ran, when the repair took the Opus
seat's pass-2 options; this file's mtime is the order proof).  Never edited after the table starts -- corrections go to
POSTTABLE16.out.

WHY.  Repair 15's pass 2 (repair15_pass2_20260926/) found the CONTROL arm's residue-text channel covered for one clear
in one latch state only.  The dedicated grok seat found H_noresetclear (the HARD_RESET branch's clear skipped: an
accepted 0x800 write also prints, and no row counted it); the Fable seat graded it L2, like the DOG pair; table 15a
measured it at 218/218.  The Opus measuring seat measured the same channel's other open cells (the DOG clear skipped
with the latch SET; the ENDIANESS clear) and proposed CONTROL-text counts on the two existing ACCEPTS sessions.  Two
consecutive passes in one class, so repair 16 closes the class in one diff: every clear the arm makes before its
residue test, in both latch states.

INSTRUMENT: crime_width_probe.table16.py = mk_r16.py (beside this file) applied to repair 15's probe f5e915f6; md5
5f770991.  226 rows = 218 + 8:
    ctlrst sw msg / sd msg         NEW session per width: 0x0001 then 0x0800 at +0x08, latch CLEAR; CONTROL-text count 1
    ctlrst sw halt / sd halt       the same sessions' RAM trip: v1 at the sentinel (the 0x0800 write reached the arm)
    rst 4w msg / rst 8w msg        the EXISTING reset sessions, now with a 0x0001 twin first: CONTROL-text count 1
    rearm ctl msg                  the EXISTING re-arm session's CONTROL-text count, 4 (ten ACCEPTS writes, latch SET)
    latch ctl msg                  the EXISTING latch session's CONTROL-text count, 4 (the same ten, latch CLEAR)
plus text: the header's {1,2} x {R,W} claim scoped to "at least one latch state", the contract's class closure and its
list of cells NOT rowed, the tl/rl rationale.  Every other session is repair 15's, unchanged; the reset sessions gain
one accepted store before their refusal.
BASELINE: dev_sgi_ip32.c 8c1d1545 (unchanged since table 12); clone /tmp/gxopus_r14, restored cmp-clean with a fresh
binary after table 15a, no .MUTANT.  The driver rebuilds base IN THE CLONE and checks [ binary -nt source ].

MUTATORS: table 14's six (md5 as in table14_20260926/logs/INSTRUMENT.md5) + mutants_16.py 8fb8c068 (H_noresetclear,
S_rst8clr, E_noendianclear, W_istlb, W_imklb, L_dogclr, L_rstclr; dry-run before this file, each a one- or two-line
edit, `base' byte-identical).  The two H/E hunks are table 15a's, and the driver cross-checks them.

