Derivations for the new rows (the first eighteen legs' other reds are carried from table 14):
  rearm ctl msg   the fixed build prints for 0x0201 and 0x0001 at both widths (4).  D_nodogclear and E_noendianclear add
                  the 0x0200 and 0x0100 texts (6); L_dogclr adds the 0x0200 texts only here, where the latch is SET (6);
                  W_ctl8w DECLINES the two latch-SET 8-byte writes that print (2).  Every refusal in this session is at
                  +0x06 (the default arm), so no decline-suppression leg reaches the CONTROL arm (M1 included).
  latch ctl msg   the same ten writes, latch CLEAR: D_nodogclear and E_noendianclear -> 6; L_dogclr, W_ctl8w keyed on
                  the latch SET -> 4.
  rst 4w/8w msg   twin 0x0001 (latch CLEAR, one text), refusal, then 0x800 (latch SET, residue 0 on the fixed build):
                  H_noresetclear and L_rstclr add the 0x800 text (2).  K_ctl4w/8w_reset_post and W_ctl8w DECLINE the
                  0x800 (their rst 4w/8w reds, as in table 14) and the count stays at the twin's 1.
  ctlrst msg      latch CLEAR throughout: H_noresetclear -> 2; nothing else reaches it (no refusal; no DOG or
                  ENDIANESS bit; the latch-keyed legs key on SET).
  ctlrst halt     S_rst8clr skips the 8-byte stop with the latch CLEAR: `ctlrst sd halt' reads 0x12345678; `rst 8w'
                  (latch SET) and `sw08 halts' (4-byte) stay green.
  W_istlb/W_imklb the only 1-byte READS at +0x10/+0x18 are each session's first refusal (latch CLEAR, the mutant still
                  declines): no row reads the cell.  Measured here so the adjudicators rule on a measurement.

CHECKS THE PRE-TABLE BLOCK OWES:
  SIBLING PARITY  After repair 16 the arm's three clears each have a residue-count row in both latch states (listed in
                  the contract block); the two TESTED bits keep their side-effect rows.  The remaining asymmetry is at
                  INTSTAT/INTMASK (width x direction x latch) and is disclosed, not rowed.
  CLAIM -> ROW    Every added sentence naming an observable maps to the rows above or to a cited measurement (table
                  15a; the Opus seat's opus_r15p2_20260926/ for the NOT-ROWED list).
  GUARD vs BODY   The new mutants' guards read len and d->warned, which the CONTROL arm's body never reads;
                  d->warned has ONE writer (the decline block).
  CHANNEL         Per new row, above; check16.py scores each named channel under each named mutant.
  ROW-LIST DIFF   The Fable seat prescribed `ctlrst sw/sd msg' with the halt as liveness: present.  The Opus seat's two
                  options: the ACCEPTS-session counts are present; the residue-VALUE text is not rowed (disclosed).

SCORING: check16.py (written before the table).  A predicted red that does not red is a FAILURE; a predicted escape that
reds is a MISS naming the rows.
